ks  thermostats appliances and much more  they can actually talk to each other  expand your range so that is great but  that actually was included with last  year's Apple TV 4K and that means that  if you go ahead and buy that base model  that is no longer included and you lose  ethernet now Apple actually made this  Apple TV 4K smaller and lighter now it's  funny that people are talking about well  you know that's a huge Improvement  obviously sarcastically because weight  doesn't matter in fact it's actually  worse because you do have cables  sticking out the back that can tug on  that now they're able to do that because  they removed the fan cooling that was in  there before and now it's fanless a lot  of people said they don't even know that  there was a fan in there because it was  so quiet and that is because they went  with the a15 which is five nanometer  it's more efficient than the a12 that we  had previously I'll talk about  performance here in just a bit and one  little weird weirdness about it but with  I would say they should definitely spend  extra 20 bucks not only to get the  storage but the extra features now with  that we have a change to the remote now  this remote they released last year  replacing that flat one and it was a  nice upgrade in my opinion but it had a  lightning connector and now we have USB  type-c which I think they should have  just done right away I don't keep  lightning cables around we use wireless  charging so when it's time to charge  it's a bit of a pain but USB type-c we  do have now I personally use Wi-Fi and  thankfully it has been improved even  though it's still Wi-Fi six it has a 2x2  mimo multiple in multiple out instead of  a one by one and sometimes in my  basement I do have issues with uh the  connection speed so that is going to be  nice now what I'm more interested is the  addition of HDR 10 plus now not  everything uses that a lot of things use  Dolby Vision but in certain apps like  YouTube for example or Amazon time you  can use HDR 10 plus and that adds extra  metadata to your HDR which makes sure  that the HR content looks its best for  your display and it could definitely  make a noticeable difference and that  was a downside previously not having  that now I would think that they could  add that in to the previous Apple TV 4K  but I guess it is just with this one now  as far as the video output this thing  has HDMI 2.1 which means it can support  4K 60 with HDR it could also support 4K  120 and AK for that connection but apple  is not allowing you to do that it is  just locked into 4K 60. now that is a  bummer because my Xbox for example it  could support 4K 120. now I don't know  if apple is going to add that in the  future for example 8K YouTube videos can  stream that but this device well  wouldn't support that with that av1 as  well and I don't think apple is probably  going to add that until they have their  own content that could support it and  then they might even lock it down to  buying a new Apple TV to do so even  though that HDMI connector can do so and  now let's talk about the a15 that is in  this device compared to the a12 in last  year's generation that is a big jump and  apple said that we're gonna get a 50  Improvement in performance for the CPU  and the graphics is a little different  now if you take a look at the scores  from those chips we had a big jump in  single core performance larger than the  50 they quoted and as far as multi-core  performance we have the same thing it is  basically double the performance with  Apple only quoting 50 now I mentioned  that we no longer have the fan in this  updated model it's just using passive  Cooling and that might be why the their  quoted performance that still sounds  great doesn't match up to the actual  test we have from these chips in other  Apple devices now when we move over to  metal if you're doing gaming decoding  all that stuff they quoted a 30  Improvement but looking at the scores  for those chips we literally have more  than double the performance comparing  the a12 to the a15 in metal and based  off of their 30 percent that they gave  which sounds good that would only bring  us up to about 7  000 estimated metal score not over 11  000 which is what the a15 is capable of  and that's the a15 in the iPhone 13  that's the four core GPU model not the  five core that came in the iPhone 13  Pros or the new iPhone 14s which are  even more powerful so why do we have  such a discrepancy in the actual  performance compared to what it should  be well I think for one we don't really  need that level of performance as I  mentioned we don't have 4K 120 out of  that HDMI it's limited 4k60 the games  aren't that difficult cold but I think  it might just be because of that passive  cooling they want sustained performance  and maybe capping it down just lowers  the power usage they think it's going to  do well enough and of course I think the  biggest change why I think of an a15  which sounds impressive but the  performance is not a 15 performance it's  just because they're Mass manufacturing  those chips the a15 costs I think less  than half of what the a16 costs and  they're no longer making devices with  the older chip so why not you know throw  that in there they're going to cap it  down maybe even there's worse performing  chips that just don't bin as well  they're going to toss that in there and  of course your device here is 129 or 149  not a very expensive you know iPad or  iPhone so with all that said who should  upgrade to this new Apple TV 4K well if  you have the HD version which they were  still selling up until now of course  that is a no-brainer and even if you  have the Apple TV 4K which I think was  2017 when that one came out it is a  no-brainer because we have so much more  formats the hardware decoding way way  better performance as well uh you cannot  do 4K 60 with HDR uh that's going to be  a really nice jump you also have the new  remote instea